# Canonical generated workspace under .cache

Move regenerable extraction, FBX conversion, Unreal staging, build
intermediates, logs, and decision data out of the repository root into one
documented `.cache/` hierarchy; keep `game/` as user-supplied source evidence
and `dist/` as final copied output instead of introducing an ambiguous
generated `assets/` root.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Migrate `extracted/`, `fbx-assets/`, `unreal-staging/`, build
  intermediates, logs, and transient decision files to stable `.cache/`
  subpaths with compatibility handling for existing local workspaces.
- [x] Update commands, manifests, tests, documentation, and validators so
  root-level legacy generated directories are no longer authoritative.
- [x] Keep `game/` outside `.cache/` because it is user-supplied source evidence
  and keep `dist/` outside `.cache/` because it is the final user
  deliverable.
- [x] Preserve resumability, provenance, deterministic hashes, and transaction
  recovery while moving paths.

## Dependencies

No explicit task dependency is required beyond the declared repository and
platform prerequisites.

## Evidence

The supported build tools keep user-supplied `game/` outside `.cache`, use
`.cache/build/data/` for versioned decisions, `.cache/build/cargo-*` for Cargo
state, and `.cache/build/run/<target>/` for Turnkey reports, UAT/UBA logs,
staging candidates, and platform build evidence. Final publication remains
`dist/<target-id>/`; no generic generated `assets/` root is introduced.

A real Windows AMD64 cook verified `UE-LocalDataCachePath` with Zen data rooted
under `.cache/build/run/windows-x64/build-hermetic-test/ddc/Zen`; UAT logs were
also redirected under that build workspace. Migration adapters now default to
`.cache/pipeline/extracted`,
`.cache/pipeline/fbx-assets`, and `.cache/pipeline/unreal-staging`. The accepted
installation, FBX, and Unreal global ledgers live at `game/manifest/game.jsonl`,
`game/manifest/fbx.jsonl`, and `game/manifest/unreal.jsonl`; package-local
transaction manifests remain with their owning package. The former root-level
generated directories are no longer ignored, so accidental recreation is
visible instead of becoming an alternate authority.

Portable identities remain unchanged: plans still carry `extracted/...`,
`fbx-assets/...`, and logical `manifest.jsonl` source tokens while MCP resolves
them to the cache workspace or `game/manifest/unreal.jsonl`. Moving the real
Unreal ledger preserved its exact SHA-256
`505d304f19859d273807233856931916e2625daa079b5a9bc1a9e9f826e0fb1c`, which
matches every published plan source-manifest revision. Extraction keeps its
sibling transaction lock under `.cache/pipeline`, FBX publication rolls back
payload and ledger together, and Unreal publication now rolls back the cache
root and central ledger together.

Default-path compatibility now migrates clean legacy extraction, complete FBX,
and Unreal workspaces into `.cache/pipeline` without changing portable
evidence identities. Extraction moves its persistent lease with the accepted
tree; FBX and Unreal move their complete generated ledgers into
`game/manifest/` with the payload root. Competing roots or manifests, active
extraction leases, interrupted extraction state, and FBX publication staging
fail closed without merging or deleting either authority. Explicit non-default
output paths remain caller-owned and are never rewritten. A default
`fbx-export-catalog` run that adopts a legacy accepted catalog stops before
rebuilding and requires an explicit removal decision; `prepare-unreal`
validates adopted evidence through the normal current gates before use.
